#. (itstool) path: chapter/title
#: C/index.docbook:234
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Innleiing"

#. (itstool) path: chapter/para
#: C/index.docbook:236
msgid ""
"This chapter introduces GTK-Doc and gives an overview of what it is and how "
"it is used."
msgstr ""
"Dette kapittelet introduserer GTK-Doc og gjev eit oversyn over kva det er og"
" korleis det vert brukt."

#. (itstool) path: sect1/title
#: C/index.docbook:242
msgid "What is GTK-Doc?"
msgstr "Kva er GTK-Doc?"

#. (itstool) path: sect1/para
#: C/index.docbook:244
msgid ""
"GTK-Doc is used to document C code. It is typically used to document the "
"public API of libraries, such as GLib-based libraries, but it can also be "
"used to document application code."
msgstr ""
"GTK-Doc vert nytta til å dokumentere C-kode. Det vert typisk nytta til å "
"dokumentere det offentlege API-et til bibliotek, slik som GLib-baserte "
"bibliotek, men det kan også nyttast til å dokumentere app-kode."

#. (itstool) path: sect1/title
#: C/index.docbook:252
msgid "How Does GTK-Doc Work?"
msgstr "Korleis fungerer GTK-Doc?"

#. (itstool) path: sect1/para
#: C/index.docbook:254
msgid ""
"GTK-Doc works by reading specially-formatted comment blocks placed inside "
"the source files to document symbols such as functions, macros, structs, "
"enums, etc. (though note that for most kind of symbols GTK-Doc will only "
"document the symbols that are declared in header files; for example it won't "
"produce output for static functions)."
msgstr ""
"GTK-Doc fungerer ved å lese spesialformaterte kommentarblokker plassert inni"
" kjeldefilene for å dokumentere symbol som funksjonar, makroar, strukturar, "
"enumerasjonar, etc. (sjølv om merk at for dei fleste symbol vil GTK-Doc "
"berre dokumentere symbola som er erklærte i header-filer; til dømes vil det "
"ikkje produsere utdata for statiske funksjonar)."

#. (itstool) path: sect1/para
#: C/index.docbook:262
msgid ""
"GTK-Doc also reads template files where documentation can be added there as "
"well."
msgstr "GTK-Doc les òg malfiler der dokumentasjon kan leggjast til."

#. (itstool) path: sect1/para
#: C/index.docbook:267
msgid ""
"GTK-Doc consists of a number of programs, each performing a different step "
"in the process."
msgstr ""
"GTK-Doc består av fleire app, kvar utfører eit ulikt steg i prosessen."

#. (itstool) path: sect1/para
#: C/index.docbook:272
msgid "The main steps are:"
msgstr "Hovudstega er:"

#. (itstool) path: listitem/para
#: C/index.docbook:279
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Writing the documentation.</guilabel> The author fills in the "
"source files with the documentation for each function, macro, structs or "
"unions, etc."
msgstr ""
"<guilabel>Skriv dokumentasjonen.</guilabel> Forfattaren fyller kjeldefilene "
"med dokumentasjon for kvar funksjon, makro, strukturar eller unionar, osv."

#. (itstool) path: listitem/para
#: C/index.docbook:288
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Gathering information about the code.</guilabel> "
"<application>gtkdoc-scan</application> scans the header files of the code "
"looking for declarations of functions, macros, enums, structs, and unions. "
"It creates the file <filename>&lt;module&gt;-decl-list.txt</filename> "
"containing a list of the declarations, placing them into sections according "
"to which header file they are in. On the first run this file is copied to "
"<filename>&lt;module&gt;-sections.txt</filename>. The author can rearrange "
"the sections, and the order of the declarations within them, to produce the "
"final desired order. The second file it generates is "
"<filename>&lt;module&gt;-decl.txt</filename>. This file contains the full "
"declarations found by the scanner. If for some reason one would like some "
"symbols to show up in the docs, where the full declaration cannot be found "
"by the scanner or the declaration should appear differently, one can place "
"entities similar to the ones in <filename>&lt;module&gt;-decl.txt</filename> "
"into <filename>&lt;module&gt;-overrides.txt</filename>."
msgstr ""
"<guilabel>Hentar informasjon om koden.</guilabel> <application>gtkdoc-"
"scan</application> skannar headerfilene i koden og ser etter deklarasjonar "
"av funksjonar, makroar, enumerasjonar, strukturar og unionar. Det lagar fila"
" <filename>&lt;module&gt;-decl-list.txt</filename> som inneheld ei liste "
"over deklarasjonane, og set dei inn i bolkar etter kva headerfil dei ligg i."
" Ved fyrste køyring vert denne fila kopiert til "
"<filename>&lt;module&gt;-sections.txt</filename>. Forfattaren kan flytte om "
"på bolkane, og rekkjefølgja på deklarasjonane inni dei, for å få den "
"endelege rekkjefølgja ein ønskjer. Den andre fila det lagar er "
"<filename>&lt;module&gt;-decl.txt</filename>. Denne fila inneheld dei fulle "
"deklarasjonane som skannaren finn. Om ein av ein eller annan grunn ønskjer "
"at enkelte symbol skal dukke opp i dokumentasjonen, der den fulle "
"deklarasjonen ikkje kan finnast av skannaren eller deklarasjonen skal sjå "
"annleis ut, kan ein setje inn entitetar som liknar på dei i "
"<filename>&lt;module&gt;-decl.txt</filename> i "
"<filename>&lt;module&gt;-overrides.txt</filename>."

#. (itstool) path: listitem/para
#: C/index.docbook:308
msgid ""
"<application>gtkdoc-scangobj</application> can also be used to dynamically "
"query a library about any GObject subclasses it exports. It saves "
"information about each object's position in the class hierarchy and about "
"any GObject properties and signals it provides."
msgstr ""
"<application>gtkdoc-scangobj</application> kan òg brukast til å spørje eit "
"bibliotek dynamisk om alle GObject-underråder det eksporterer. Det lagrar "
"informasjon om kvar objekts plassering i klassestrukturen og om alle "
"GObject-eigenskapar og signal det tilbyr."

#. (itstool) path: listitem/para
#: C/index.docbook:314
msgid ""
"<application>gtkdoc-scanobj</application> should not be used anymore. It was "
"needed in the past when GObject was still GtkObject inside GTK."
msgstr ""
"<application>gtkdoc-scanobj</application> bør ikkje brukast lenger. Det var "
"nødvendig i fortida då GObject framleis var GtkObject inne i GTK."

#. (itstool) path: listitem/para
#: C/index.docbook:322
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Generating the XML and HTML/PDF.</guilabel> <application>gtkdoc-"
"mkdb</application> turns the template files into XML files in the <filename "
"class=\"directory\">xml/</filename> subdirectory. If the source code "
"contains documentation for symbols, using the special comment blocks, it "
"gets merged in here. If there are no tmpl files used it only reads docs from "
"sources and introspection data."
msgstr ""
"<guilabel>Lagar XML og HTML/PDF.</guilabel> <application>gtkdoc-"
"mkdb</application> gjer malfilene om til XML-filer i undermappa <filename "
"class=\"directory\">xml/</filename>. Dersom kjeldekoden inneheld "
"dokumentasjon for symbol, ved bruk av dei spesielle kommentarblokkene, vert "
"dette slått saman her. Dersom det ikkje vert brukt tmpl-filer, les han berre"
" dokumentasjon frå kjelder og introspeksjonsdata."

#. (itstool) path: listitem/para
#: C/index.docbook:332
msgid ""
"<application>gtkdoc-mkhtml</application> turns the XML files into HTML files "
"in the <filename class=\"directory\">html/</filename> subdirectory. Likewise "
"<application>gtkdoc-mkpdf</application> turns the XML files into a PDF "
"document called <filename>&lt;package&gt;.pdf</filename>."
msgstr ""
"<application>gtkdoc-mkhtml</application> gjer om XML-filene til HTML-filer i"
" undermappa <filename class=\"directory\">html/</filename>. På same måte "
"gjer <application>gtkdoc-mkpdf</application> om XML-filene til eit PDF-"
"dokument kalla <filename>&lt;package&gt;.pdf</filename>."

#. (itstool) path: listitem/para
#: C/index.docbook:339
msgid ""
"Files in <filename class=\"directory\">xml/</filename> and <filename "
"class=\"directory\">html/</filename> directories are always overwritten. One "
"should never edit them directly."
msgstr ""
"Filer i <filename class=\"directory\">xml/</filename> og <filename "
"class=\"directory\">html/</filename> mapper vert alltid overskrivne. Ein bør"
" aldri redigere dei direkte."

#. (itstool) path: listitem/para
#: C/index.docbook:347
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Fixing up cross-references between documents.</guilabel> After "
"installing the HTML files, <application>gtkdoc-fixxref</application> can be "
"run to fix up any cross-references between separate documents. For example, "
"the GTK documentation contains many cross-references to types documented in "
"the GLib manual."
msgstr ""
